<!--
  A fixture report for the instrumented test floor's positive control.

  It has the shape of the real run — eight classes, twenty-six tests, none
  skipped — so the control can run the gate against a report that MEETS the
  floor and fail it by moving the floor, rather than by having no report at all.

  It must match the floor in `config/docs/instrumented-test-floor.txt`
  EXACTLY, and that is sharper than it was when this fixture was written. The
  floor ratchets: a report that delivers fewer classes or tests than the floor
  records is a dropped floor, and a report that delivers more is a floor that
  is behind the suite. Either one fails the gate on a clean tree, so a fixture
  that is off by one class in either direction proves nothing and breaks the
  control that reads it.

  The classes and their sizes are the ones the instrumented suite actually
  has, so the fixture stays a picture of the suite and not of a guess about it.

  When the floor moves, this fixture has to move with it.
-->
